<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonçalo da Silveira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1526–1561</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonçalo da Silveira was a Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missionary who in 1560–1561 travelled to the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwene-mutapa">Mwene Mutapa</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> and baptised the king and members of his family. Muslim traders at the court persuaded the king that the missionary was a spy and sorcerer, and Silveira was strangled in March 1561. His death was later used to justify the Portuguese expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-barreto">Francisco Barreto</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goncalo-da-silveira.jpg" alt="Gonçalo da Silveira" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Author : Adrien Melaer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martyrdom_by_strangulation_of_Jesuit_Father_Gon%C3%A7alo_da_Silveira_in_Monomotapa_1561.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
